media: h713-hdmirx: say when the status file is reading our own record

The debugfs status file reads the signal information record afresh on every
open, and 0136n gave it two decoded lines, `colour:` and `hdr:`. Both are
honest about what the record says and silent about whose record it is.

Under a standing picture it is ours. The display side republishes the VidDec
descriptor (0117), the firmware answers by writing that descriptor's values
into the record, and from then on the record carries the descriptor's
constants - colour format 0, exactly 30.00 Hz - and not the HDMI signal's.
h713_hdmirx_detect_timings() has recognised that since 0136f and tightened
the test with desc_seen in 0136o; the status file never learned it.

Measured on the HY310 on 22.09.2026 with the debug kernel
(umbau/test-20260915/dev20-20260922.md, row "Q3 status file"): with a
1024x768 PC timing standing on the wall, `signal-info` read signal_id 19,
30.00 Hz, color_format 0, color_space 1, full_range 0, so the `colour:` line
said "limited range" - while G_FMT went on reporting the full range that the
genuine record had carried, because 0136n caches the colour and writes the
cache only from a genuine record. Two lines of the same file disagreeing,
and the one that looks live is the wrong one.

The same run also settled the question 0136o left open: signal_id is 19 for
the own record as well, the genuine 720p value, so the record alone does not
tell the two apart and the test stays detect_timings' three terms.

This patch adds one line under the two, printed only in that state:

  colour:       BT.709, limited range, progressive, DVI/PC source (...)
  hdr:          Sdr (hdr_mode 0) -- ...
                (own record - the source's values are the cached ones:
                 BT.709, full range)

The cached pair is named through h713_hdmirx_colour_map read backwards, the
same table 0136n fills the cache from, so the wording of the two lines
matches. Nothing else changes: the raw words, the decoded record line and
both decoded lines are printed exactly as before, no state is written, and
the driver's behaviour outside debugfs is untouched.

Source: umbau/test-20260915/dev20-20260922.md (row "Q3 status file" and the
debug-kernel table), umbau/work/Q3/REPORT.txt sections 1.3 and 1.5.
Follow-up to 0136n and 0136o; both stay byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
@@ -4304,6 +4304,18 @@ static const char *h713_hdmirx_hdr_note(u32 hdr_mode)
 	return "";
 }
 
+/* 0136n's map read backwards: the name the cached fmt_* pair came from. */
+static const char *h713_hdmirx_cached_colour(const struct h713_hdmirx *rx)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(h713_hdmirx_colour_map); i++)
+		if (h713_hdmirx_colour_map[i].colorspace == rx->fmt_colorspace &&
+		    h713_hdmirx_colour_map[i].ycbcr_enc == rx->fmt_ycbcr_enc)
+			return h713_hdmirx_colour_map[i].name;
+	return "unknown";
+}
+
 static void h713_hdmirx_show_signal_info(struct seq_file *s,
 					 struct h713_hdmirx *rx)
 {
@@ -4352,6 +4364,19 @@ static void h713_hdmirx_show_signal_info(struct seq_file *s,
 		   h713_hdmirx_hdr_scheme[sig.hdr_mode] ?
 			h713_hdmirx_hdr_scheme[sig.hdr_mode] : "unnamed",
 		   sig.hdr_mode, h713_hdmirx_hdr_note(sig.hdr_mode));
+
+	/*
+	 * Under a standing picture the record is the descriptor we published:
+	 * 1024x768 read "limited" there while G_FMT kept the genuine record's
+	 * full range (dev20, row "Q3 status file"). detect_timings()' test.
+	 */
+	if (sig.color_format == 0 && READ_ONCE(rx->desc_seen) &&
+	    sig.frame_rate_x100 == H713_OWN_RECORD_FPS_X100)
+		seq_printf(s,
+			   "              (own record - the source's values are the cached ones: %s, %s range)\n",
+			   h713_hdmirx_cached_colour(rx),
+			   rx->fmt_quantization == V4L2_QUANTIZATION_FULL_RANGE ?
+				"full" : "limited");
 }
 
 /*
